sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: stage 4 of the command development pipeline (feature-flow sections 3 to 5). The author opens the PR and turns on auto-merge; CI alone decides; the merge queue lands it when Required checks pass. A change to command code also needs the Proofs check of stage 5.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: development pipeline stage 4 · PR with fast CI
  %% kind: pipeline.4-pr-fast-ci
  autonumber
  %% lane AG icon=terminal pill=author tone=gray
  %% lane GH icon=server pill=PR tone=blue
  %% lane CI icon=workflow pill=checks tone=green
  %% lane MN icon=server pill=lands tone=amber
  participant AG as Author agent<br/>as nckrtl
  participant GH as GitHub<br/>PR · merge queue
  participant CI as Fast CI<br/>hosted runners
  participant MN as main<br/>branch
  AG->>GH: Push the branch<br/>proof passed first
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - the cases passed on the nested fleet (stage 3)
  AG->>GH: Open the PR<br/>one change
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - one PR per change, with the chart, page and cases already merged for a command (stage 1)
  AG->>GH: Turn on auto-merge<br/>gh pr merge --auto
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - the author runs it as `nckrtl`, so the PR joins the merge queue once CI passes
  %%> Why:
  %%> - a bot's auto-merge never queues; CI alone decides the merge
  GH->>CI: Start the checks<br/>on the PR head
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - GitHub runs `ci.yml` on hosted runners for the PR head
  Note over CI: Scope the change<br/>changed files pick the jobs
  %%> Rules:
  %%> - documentation only (`docs/`, `*.md`, charts): docs checks only, never a VM job
  %%> - Gateway code: fast checks and the Gateway Pest suite
  %%> - web or CLI code: fast checks and that build
  %%> - command code (workflows, extensions, playbooks, roles, versions): fast checks and the VM job `Proofs` (stage 5)
  Note over CI: Fast checks<br/>about 1 minute
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - runs the required job set `Required checks`; every main commit also builds the web artifact and `Gateway release inputs` for the release (stage 6)
  alt Required checks pass
    CI-->>GH: Checks green<br/>PR enters the queue
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the PR joins the merge queue because auto-merge is on
    GH->>CI: Test the combined commit<br/>merge queue run
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - the queue builds the PR on top of the newest main and runs the same selection rule
    %%> - a batch needs the VM job only for PRs that change command code
    CI-->>GH: Combined commit green
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the queue run tested the exact commit it now puts on main
    GH->>MN: Land the PR<br/>merge queue
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the commit is on main; the Gateway release (stage 6) finds it
  else a check fails
    CI--xGH: Checks red<br/>PR stays out of the queue
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the author fixes and pushes again; auto-merge stays on and the queue takes the PR when it is green
    %%> - a red combined commit removes the PR from the queue
  end
  Note over GH: Proofs check<br/>command code only
  %%> Not built:
  %%> - the required check `Proofs` (stage 5); today the queue needs `Required checks` alone
